{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129752",
      "title": "Updating Form Values Programmatically",
      "lectureOrder": 250,
      "videoOrder": 238,
      "sourceHash": "210b4216bec725cc2e083c7f7a6ca66922c3dab6569079dacc3dc8f1f4658a56",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.33,
          "en": "So how can we use the saved value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "to pre-populate the form?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.72,
          "en": "Well, we can also do that here in afterNextRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.72,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "before setting up that subscription, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 17.31,
          "en": "Here we can access local storage to read a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.31,
          "end": 19.32,
          "en": "from it with getItem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.32,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "And I then use the same key as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 24.873,
          "en": "to read any value stored under that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "And that will be my saved form, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "the saved form information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "So in my case, it won't be an object in this shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "though we'll actually get it as a string value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 43.04,
          "en": "So I actually need to parse that with JSON parse like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "Now that could be undefined here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "And therefore what I'll actually do is I'll add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 55.77,
          "en": "and check if savedForm is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.77,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "So if I got some value from local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 63.299,
          "en": "and in that case I'll get my loadedFormData, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.299,
          "end": 66.837,
          "en": "from JSON parse savedForm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 72.78,
          "en": "So that should now be an object in this shape here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "So my saved email can be extracted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 78.303,
          "en": "from loadedFormData.email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "and then we just need to update the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.2,
          "en": "with that saved value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 89.49,
          "en": "Well, and as it turns out, this form object that is set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "by Angular does have methods that do allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 98.36,
          "en": "to change the values that are managed by those controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 103.64,
          "en": "because this form object gives you a set value method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "And this does what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 111.363,
          "en": "It sets the overall form value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "Now of course, you need to pass that new value to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "And here for the overall form, that would be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 123.83,
          "en": "that has a email key, which should be set to some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 127.8,
          "en": "and a password key that should be set to some value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.8,
          "end": 131.19,
          "en": "And of course the email should be set to the saved email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.19,
          "end": 134.07,
          "en": "The password will be an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "Alternatively, if we only wanna update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "one of these two fields, as it's the case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 142.59,
          "en": "we can also access our controls here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.59,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "And then here are the email control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "and call set value on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "And then I don't pass an object to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 151.773,
          "en": "but instead the saved email itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "So that would work as well if you don't wanna update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 158.043,
          "en": "the entire form, but just one control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 163.503,
          "en": "Now if you save that, you'll get an error, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 166.98,
          "en": "that you cannot read the properties of undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 169.07999999999998,
          "en": "when using setValue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "And the problem here again, is that whilst the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 176.55,
          "en": "has been rendered here and the form object is initialized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 181.55,
          "en": "the control objects actually aren't fully initialized yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 181.86,
          "end": 185.67,
          "en": "So trying to call setValue on one doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 185.67,
          "end": 188.31,
          "en": "or trying to set those control values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.31,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "in general doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "And the work around here with the template driven approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 200,
          "en": "would be to use set timeout to set a very short timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.61,
          "end": 204.32999999999998,
          "en": "of one millisecond to essentially just wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.32999999999998,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "for one update tick that's performed behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "because then the firm will be fully initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.73,
          "en": "and we'll see a more elegant solution for this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.73,
          "end": 219.9,
          "en": "later once we deal with reactive forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.9,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "But here, this is a quick and easy workaround",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 226.02,
          "en": "that does allow us to update the form now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 229.35,
          "en": "So with this in place, you'll see the error is gone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.35,
          "end": 232.38,
          "en": "and you see it was pre-populated here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 232.38,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "And if I go to the application tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 237.72,
          "en": "and I delete saved log in the form and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.72,
          "end": 240.003,
          "en": "you see it's not pre-populated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 241.02,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "but if I now start typing here again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 246.96,
          "en": "and then for some reason I stop typing like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.96,
          "end": 250.08,
          "en": "and I reload, this state was saved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.08,
          "end": 252.87,
          "en": "and is pre-populated again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.87,
          "end": 255,
          "en": "So that's now how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255,
          "end": 258.15,
          "en": "And of course, submitting also still works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.15,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "And with that, we now added this nice extra feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "And along the way you learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 268.38,
          "en": "more interesting form capabilities and features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.38,
          "end": 271.98,
          "en": "like value changes and like setValue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.98,
          "end": 275.97,
          "en": "which are all provided by Angular because Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 275.97,
          "end": 278.90999999999997,
          "en": "is managing this form object for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 278.90999999999997,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "And as you can tell here, when using template driven forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 286.14,
          "en": "it does all that for you with very little work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 286.14,
          "end": 287.433,
          "en": "from your site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 293.25,
          "en": "All you do is register inputs in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.25,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "and you did add the forms module, but that's then it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 300.72,
          "en": "The rest is done by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 300.72,
          "end": 304.47,
          "en": "And therefore, template driven forms are a nice way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 304.47,
          "end": 309.47,
          "en": "of setting up forms quick and easy, without too much work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 309.51,
          "end": 313.83,
          "en": "But they do come with certain downsides, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 313.83,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "this workaround, which we had to use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 320.46,
          "en": "and that's why now we'll move on to reactive forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.46,
          "end": 324.09,
          "en": "and we'll learn about this alternative way of creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 324.09,
          "end": 327.453,
          "en": "and registering and using forms with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
